sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To find the first apotome.
----
proof:

Set out a rational straight line, and let {BG} be commensurable in length with {A}. Then {BG} is also rational.

Set out two square numbers {DE} and {EF}, and let their difference {FD|DF} not be square. Then {ED|DE} does not have to {DF} the ratio which a square number has to a square number.

Let it be contrived that {ED|DE} is to {DF} as the square on {BG} is to the square on {GC}. Then the square on {BG} is commensurable with the square on {GC}. [!just X.6.Cor; X.6]

But the square on {BG} is rational, therefore the square on {GC} is also rational. Therefore {GC} is also rational.

